# 10. KNOWLEDGE LIFECYCLE MANAGEMENT

This is the defining feature of the project.

The platform should continuously manage approved institutional knowledge.

Support these lifecycle actions:

## CREATE

Create knowledge from newly uploaded institutional documents.

## KEEP

Recommend KEEP when:

- The current article remains accurate.
- The source policy has not been replaced.
- The information is still applicable.
- The review date has not indicated a required change.

## UPDATE

Recommend UPDATE when:

- A new document version is uploaded.
- Fee amounts change.
- Academic dates change.
- Admission deadlines change.
- Examination rules change.
- Scholarship conditions change.
- The original information is incomplete or superseded.

Compare the old and new document versions.

Show exactly what changed.

## RETIRE

Recommend RETIRE when:

- A policy has expired.
- An old notice has been replaced.
- A programme is no longer offered.
- A rule is no longer applicable.
- A document is explicitly withdrawn.

Never permanently delete previous knowledge.

Keep archived versions and historical records.

All important lifecycle decisions must be proposals.

A Human Reviewer must approve an update or retirement action before it becomes effective.

Include a review schedule for documents with upcoming review or expiry dates.

